# Cursor rules

This repo is `CSweet.Office.Contracts` — dependency-light wire contracts shared by C-Sweet Headquarters and C-Sweet Office.

Follow `AGENTS.md` and the `docs/` reference (`README.md` index, `control-plane.md`, `guest-broker.md`, `workloads.md`, `security.md`, `versioning.md`).

- Scope: cross-process messages, workload specs, protocol constants, framing, signature canonicalization only. No provider interfaces, RuntimeHost RPC, persistence, scheduling, or virtualization.
- SemVer: breaking wire/public API → major; additive → minor; fix → patch. Sync Office + Headquarters pins.
- `AssignmentEnvelope` bytes are frozen (pinned by `AssignmentEncodingCompatibilityTests`). Any canonical-bytes change needs a major bump plus a new vector test.
- Preserve unknown protobuf fields; keep new fields optional/back-compatible (`OfficeVersion` pattern).
- Never emit secrets (receipts, handoff secrets, boot tokens, nonces, `artifact_read_token`) into logs, status, or examples.
- Validate with `dotnet test CSweet.Office.Contracts.slnx -c Release`, `dotnet pack ... -o artifacts/packages`, and package-only `dotnet test ... /p:UseLocalIsolation=false`; inspect the `.nupkg` before handoff.
